[1;33m[WARN][0m   Review: changes_requested (9 issue(s)) — The implementation partially addresses the prescribed root cause: live_preview config IS present in the Stack options, ICommonContentstackConfig DOES include the live_preview field, and setCommonConfig DOES call query.includeFallback() when preview is enabled. However, the change is incomplete in critical ways. (1) No @contentstack/live-preview-utils dependency is installed — the client-side SDK required for real-time preview subscriptions is absent. (2) No reactive ContentstackProvider component exists — useContent still reads from a static context value, so even if preview events fired, no re-render would propagate to the 236+ consuming components. (3) Stack.livePreview() is never called to initialize the client-side preview subsystem. (4) No vitest unit tests exist for any aspect of the live preview feature. As a result, 6 of 8 acceptance criteria related to real-time updates without page reload, successive edits appearing live, and connection-drop resilience are unmet. The server-side draft-fetching capability is in place, but the client-side reactivity mechanism — the other half of the prescribed fix — is entirely missing. Verdict: changes_requested.

